WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.475
Privacy and training are
the agency's, end to end.

2
00:00:03.475 --> 00:00:07.926
NIST's privacy baseline applies whatever
the impact level, so a Low system

3
00:00:07.926 --> 00:00:12.450
holding the same personal information
carries the same privacy controls.

4
00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.572
No privacy control
carries a FedRAMP class,

5
00:00:15.572 --> 00:00:19.475
and none of the 2026 indicator
themes is about privacy.

6
00:00:19.475 --> 00:00:23.581
The controls ask by what authority
the agency collects the information,

7
00:00:23.581 --> 00:00:26.045
for what purpose, whether
it told the person,

8
00:00:26.045 --> 00:00:29.125
and whether it published the
system of records notice.

9
00:00:29.125 --> 00:00:31.605
The senior agency official for privacy

10
00:00:31.605 --> 00:00:34.687
approves the privacy plan
before authorization.

11
00:00:34.687 --> 00:00:38.513
Training is the one family
no configuration can close.

12
00:00:38.513 --> 00:00:42.657
OMB's Circular A-130 requires
training before access,

13
00:00:42.657 --> 00:00:46.425
and OPM's rule sets an
annual floor for awareness.

14
00:00:46.425 --> 00:00:49.994
Social engineering awareness
is required at Moderate;

15
00:00:49.994 --> 00:00:53.563
phishing exercises are
optional, tailored in by choice.

16
00:00:53.563 --> 00:00:58.599
A dashboard showing 98 percent completion
is a number with no denominator.

17
00:00:58.599 --> 00:01:02.573
The proof is counts per population,
measured against a stated roster,

18
00:01:02.573 --> 00:01:05.570
which someone who didn't
produce them can re-derive.
